ICHTING MATHEMATISCH CENTRUM BE LIABLE\nFOR ANY SPECIAL, INDIRECT OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES\nWHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN\nACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT\nOF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.\n"},{"name":"Atelier Companion Art","version":"1.1","license":"LicenseRef-Atelier-Companion-Art","text":"# Atelier Companion Art License\n\nVersion 1.1\n\nCopyright © 2026 Senne Chin, trading as Chinnovations (the Netherlands). All rights reserved, except as granted below.\n\nIn this licence, \"Chinnovations\" means Senne Chin, trading as Chinnovations, and whoever the rights in the Companion\nArt pass to (section 7).\n\nAtelier's code, including the companion engine, is open source under the [Mozilla Public License 2.0](LICENSE). The\ncompanion art is not: it is licensed under these terms, so that the Atelier characters stay Atelier's while everyone can\ncreate with them inside Atelier.\n\n## 1. What this licence covers\n\n\"Companion Art\" means:\n\n- the files in `src/renderer/public/companion/` (character parts, rigs, face layers, configuration and presets);\n- the recipes in `scripts/companion-assets/` that generate those files;\n- the files in `branding/official/` that depict an Atelier character (listed in `branding/official/LICENSE.md`), and the\n  scripts that draw them: `scripts/app-icons/art.mjs`, `scripts/app-icons/render-pip.mjs` and `scripts/app-icons/pip/`;\n- everything generated from the above: models, textures, images, renders and animations;\n- the Atelier characters Pip, Juniper, Bolt, Mochi, Sage and Pepper (their names, looks and personalities), and any\n  character assembled from the Companion Art.\n\nEvery other file in this repository is licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0.\n\n## 2. What you may do\n\nFree of charge, worldwide, you may:\n\n1. **Build and develop Atelier.** Use, copy and modify the Companion Art to build, run, test and develop Atelier from this\n   repository, and contribute your changes to the Atelier project. You may also share builds made from this repository,\n   with or without changes, with others so they can test or review changes for the Atelier project: for example\n   pull-request previews, builds for testers and CI artifacts.\n2. **Create characters for Atelier.** Make companions with Atelier from the Companion Art, and use, share and distribute them\n   (for example as `.ateliercompanion` files) for use with Atelier.\n3. **Make things for Atelier.** Include the Companion Art, or characters made from it, in packs, apps, worlds and other\n   content made for Atelier and distributed for use within Atelier, including content you sell.\n4. **Give your brand a mascot inside Atelier.** A character you make from the Companion Art (with a name and personality\n   of your own, not one of the Atelier characters) may be the mascot or face of your brand, product or organisation\n   inside Atelier: for example the companion that represents you in your pack, app or world.\n5. **Show it.** Use images and recordings of these characters in screenshots, videos, streams, tutorials, reviews,\n   articles, fan art and store listings about Atelier, or about things made for Atelier, including promotion of your own\n   content for Atelier.\n6. **Pass on official builds** as described in [TRADEMARKS.md](TRADEMARKS.md).\n\n## 3. What you may not do\n\nWithout written permission from Chinnovations, you may not:\n\n1. use the Companion Art, or characters made from it, in other software, or in a build of Atelier that you distribute\n   as your own product (a fork), modified or not: a fork or another product brings its own character designs in place\n   of the Companion Art (the engine is MPL-2.0, so it can load them). Sharing builds to test or review changes for the\n   Atelier project is allowed by section 2.1;\n2. use the Companion Art, or characters made from it, as a mascot, logo, icon or brand character outside Atelier: in your\n   own apps, websites, products, merchandise or services, or as the identity of a fork or a new brand (showing it\n   as allowed in section 2.5 is fine);\n3. use the Atelier characters themselves (Pip, Juniper, Bolt, Mochi, Sage and Pepper) as the mascot of anyone else's\n   brand, product or organisation, inside or outside Atelier;\n4. sell or license the Companion Art on its own, or present it as your own work.\n\n## 4. Trademarks\n\nThe Atelier characters are also trademarks; see [TRADEMARKS.md](TRADEMARKS.md). This licence does not grant trademark\nrights beyond saying truthfully that something is made for Atelier or uses Atelier characters.\n\n## 5. Contributions\n\nWhen you contribute to the Companion Art, you confirm that you have the right to do so. You keep the copyright in\nyour contribution, and you grant Chinnovations a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free and irrevocable\nlicence to use, reproduce, modify, distribute and sublicense it, under this licence, any later version of it or other\nterms Chinnovations chooses. Chinnovations may transfer this licence together with the Companion Art.\n\n## 6. No warranty, and ending the licence\n\nThe Companion Art is provided \"as is\", without warranty of any kind. If you break these terms, your rights under this\nlicence end automatically; they come back if you stop within 30 days of being told.\n\n## 7. Who holds this licence, and new versions\n\nChinnovations may transfer the Companion Art, with its rights under this licence, for example to a company that\ncontinues Atelier or to a buyer of Atelier. Whoever receives them takes Chinnovations' place in this licence, and the\npermissions you already have stay valid.\n\nChinnovations may publish new versions of this licence, each with its own version number. Companion Art you received\nunder one version stays available to you under that version, and you may also follow any later version.\n\nQuestions or requests for permission: Chinnovations, [contact@chinnovations.nl](mailto:contact@chinnovations.nl).\n"},{"name":"body-parser","version":"2.4.0","license":"MIT","text":"(The MIT License)\n\nCopyright (c) 2014 Jonathan Ong <me@jongleberry.com>\nCopyright (c) 2014-2015 Douglas Christopher Wilson <doug@somethingdoug.com>\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining\na copy of this software and associated documentation files (the\n'Software'), to deal in the Software without restriction, including\nwithout limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,\ndistribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to\npermit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to\nthe following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be\nincluded in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED 'AS IS', WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,\nEXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF\nMERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.\nIN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY\nCLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT,\nTORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE\nSOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n"},{"name":"builder-util-runtime","version":"9.7.0","license":"MIT","text":"The MIT License (MIT)\n\nCopyright (c) 2015 Loopline Systems\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notic